  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Transforming livelihoods through the honey trade in Mozambique</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">For thousands of families in central Mozambique, increasing honey production and quality offers a potential new source of income. Beekeepers need better technical skills, help to organise themselves into associations, and a channel to national and international organic honey markets. This project will support 5,000 beekeepers in two provinces of Central Region to produce better quality honey with advice from specialist production experts. They will be helped to sell this through a new honey marketing company which will be 45%-owned by a representative beekeeper&apos;s union, with guidance from an experiencing advisor in cooperative management. Improved production, organisation and access to markets will significantly improve income at the family level, as well as building the knowledge and skills of farmers. The project will reduce deforestation by switching from bark hives to modern hives.</narrative>
  </description>
